4. IAMScene
Public
0.1.2
Independent release train

Path: packages/iamscene/






















9











What it is: Your portable, editable 3D scene format and runtime.

This is not just a renderer or a collection of 3D assets.

It defines a common format that different applications can create, edit, validate, animate and display.

The native file extension is:

*.iamscene.json
What a scene contains
A scene document can describe:
- Scene identity and metadata.
- Node hierarchy.
- Object transforms.
- Geometry provenance.
- Materials.
- Asset references.
- Cameras.
- Environments.
- Animation tracks.
- Declarative interactions.
The format uses a right-handed, Y-up coordinate system with meters as its default unit.

It has stable identities for scene nodes, materials, assets, animations and interactions.

It also prohibits executable JavaScript inside scene documents.
The actual API
The package exposes six major API areas:
Module	Responsibility
types.ts	Scene data types
document.ts	Creation and serialization
validate.ts	Document validation
editor.ts	Scene editing
animation.ts	Time-based animation
runtime.ts	Browser scene presentation

For example:
import {
  createSceneDocument,
  createSceneEditor,
  parseSceneDocument,
  validateSceneDocument
} from '@inneranimalmedia/iamscene';

const scene = createSceneDocument({
  id: 'product-world',
  name: 'Product World'
});

const editor = createSceneEditor(scene);

editor.addNode({
  id: 'hero-group',
  name: 'Hero Group',
  kind: 'group',
  parentId: 'scene-root',
  visible: true,
  transform: {
    position: [0, 0, 0],
    rotation: [0, 0, 0, 1],
    scale: [1, 1, 1]
  }
});

const saved = editor.serialize();
const reopened = parseSceneDocument(saved);

if (!validateSceneDocument(reopened).valid) {
  throw new Error('Invalid scene');
}


The OCCT connection
This is one of the most important features.

IAMScene integrates with your canonical:
- agentsam-occt
- agentsam-3d-viewer
The package includes both as bundled dependencies.

Its native geometry pipeline can generate:
Output	Purpose
GLTF	Presentation geometry
STEP	Interoperable geometry
BREP	Native geometry representation
SHA-256	Asset integrity and provenance

The canonical geometry feature history stays in the scene document.

The GLTF is not treated as the only source of truth.

This is exactly the kind of foundation that can connect CAD Creator, SamSketch, robotics visualization and creative production without requiring every application to invent its own scene format.
Existing integration points
I found references in:
- apps/samsketch/src/native-scene-editor.ts
- apps/samsketch/src/main.ts
- packages/theme-scenes
- apps/local-studio/backend/worker/work-samsketch-scenes.js
There are also three example projects:
1. Original circuit hover scene.
2. Retrofuturistic circuit loop.
3. Scroll-controlled circuit.
The package has 23 explicit test cases across seven test files. That is a test inventory, not a claim that all 23 have passed in this audit.
What IAMScene is NOT
It does not replace:
- A native parametric CAD project.
- A complete BIM project.
- A video timeline.
- A physics simulation.
- A game save-state.
It can represent or present scenes associated with those systems, but those systems retain their own authoritative data.

For example, a Franka robot visualization could use IAMScene to represent its environment and objects. That does not make IAMScene the robot's motion controller or safety system.
Why it is version 0.1.2
Unlike the three packages above, IAMScene explicitly declares:

"releaseTrain": "independent"

It is also public, has a declared FSL-1.1-MIT license, and has public npm distribution configured.

Its 0.1.2 version is therefore not necessarily a stale 2.6.15 package. It is independently versioned.

Its AgentSam catalog still describes it as in-development and needs-review, which is a separate maturity classification.

5. How these four packages work together
This is where the distinction becomes useful.
PrimeTech

Professional creative and engineering products

Architectural Intelligence

Understands materials, specifications, references and architectural requirements.


PrimeTech Procedures

Executes controlled, repeatable engineering workflows.


IAMScene

Defines, edits and presents portable spatial scenes.


Theme Contract

Makes CMS themes compatible with customer-owned content.




AgentSam shared infrastructure

Identity · Authorization · Operations · Assets · Runtime · Distribution


Here is how I would classify their ownership:
Package	Primary owner	Distribution
Architectural Intelligence	PrimeTech Architecture	AgentSam capability
PrimeTech Procedures	PrimeTech Engineering	Internal shared package
Theme Contract	AgentSam CMS	Internal shared package
IAMScene	PrimeTech Spatial / Creative	Public developer package

6. What I would actually change
My recommendations are:
Package	Action
Architectural Intelligence	Retain, expand real operations, prepare public distribution
PrimeTech Procedures	Retain private, expand verified procedures, align versions
Theme Contract	Consolidate duplicate implementations immediately
IAMScene	Retain public and independent, mature its API and integrations

Keep
 IAMScene is an especially valuable foundation. I would not merge it into CAD Creator or bury it inside PrimeTech Procedures.

Keep
 PrimeTech Procedures should become the reusable execution layer, not another application or runtime.

Reconcile
 Theme Contract has the clearest immediate architectural defect: two same-named private packages with different contents.

Expand
 Architectural Intelligence has a good foundation, but its current five MCP operations are substantially smaller than the twelve architectural skills might suggest.

My biggest recommendation: Treat these as four distinct assets with four distinct ownership boundaries. They complement one another; they should not be collapsed into a single PrimeTech package.

The next thing I would investigate is the actual dependency graph between these four packages and CAD Creator, SamSketch, the CMS and Local Studio, so we can identify which ones are already genuinely integrated versus merely present in the monorepo.

















